@@ -110,19 +110,27 @@ fn the_machine_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page() {
 
 /// #2105: the ribbon is 22 px taller since #2027, and the machine page's
 /// action row fell under the fold of a 720 px window: the user had to
-/// scroll to reach the buttons. The row is reachable without a scroll -
-/// every action button's painted bottom sits inside the Properties leaf.
+/// scroll to reach the buttons. The page's visible bottom is NOT the
+/// bottom of the Properties leaf: `pages.rs` gives the page's ScrollArea
+/// the leaf height minus 40 px and draws the separator and the `Close`
+/// footer in that band. So the edge to measure against is the top of
+/// `Close`, read from the same pane as the buttons.
 #[test]
 fn the_machine_page_buttons_fit_without_scrolling_at_720_px() {
     let mut h = shell_harness();
     open_machine(&mut h, Some("Tormach 770MX"));
-    let leaf = super::layout::leaf_rect(&h.state().dock, &Tab::Properties).expect("the properties leaf");
-    assert!(top(&h, GROUPS[2]) < leaf.bottom(), "the action group title is in the fold: {:?} {leaf:?}", rect(&h, GROUPS[2]));
+    let close = h
+        .get_by_role_and_label(egui::accesskit::Role::Pane, "Properties")
+        .query_by_label("Close")
+        .expect("the Close footer of the Properties pane")
+        .rect();
+    let title = rect(&h, GROUPS[2]);
+    assert!(title.top() < close.top(), "the action group title is in the fold: {title:?} vs Close {close:?}");
     for label in ["Load other", "Edit", "Clear"] {
         let r = rect(&h, label);
         assert!(
-            r.bottom() <= leaf.bottom() + 0.5,
-            "{label} {r:?} falls under the fold of the Properties leaf {leaf:?}"
+            r.bottom() <= close.top() + 1.0,
+            "{label} {r:?} stands below the page's visible bottom - the Close footer {close:?} starts there"
         );
     }
 }

From b810c98a7c5982c91b5c68f4c142f895c88ef1a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:13:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(ui): the machine action row stands above the visible
 bottom at 720 px

A review found the first fix (Refresh beside the Library combo) was not
enough: the "Load other", "Edit" and "Clear" row still ended 20 px below
the top of the pane's Close footer, so the buttons were outside the page.
Moving the Library row one row up cannot pay for 26 px.

The page now reclaims the height in three places, and keeps every label,
word and command:

- machine_page draws its rows at a 2 px vertical gap of its own (ROW_GAP)
  instead of the shell's 3 px. The gap is set on the page's own Ui, which
  the scroll area rebuilds each frame, so no other page changes.
- The machine overview readout uses a 2 px row gap (OVERVIEW_GAP).
  machine_grid takes the row gap as a parameter; the machine editor
  header keeps its 4 px (machine_grid::ROW_GAP).
- The two prose lines of the ownership block (setup_pages::ownership) are
  drawn small and dimmed, like the machine page's own help line. In the
  274 px pane each wrapped to three lines of 15 px; each now takes two
  lines of 10 px. Their words and AccessKit labels are unchanged.

Measured in shell_harness() at 1280x720, Tormach 770MX loaded. The
Properties leaf spans y = 104..682 and the Close footer starts at
y = 648. The action row moved from y = 644..668 (below the footer edge)
to y = 570..594. The pin test
the_machine_page_buttons_fit_without_scrolling_at_720_px is green; so
are the machine page behaviour tests and layout_page_setup_machine.

docs/decisions/2105-machine-buttons-720.md is corrected: the page's
buttons are "Load other", "Edit" and "Clear" (the file named a button
"New", which does not exist), and it states the measured result.
